    "https://fa-ewic-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/168": {
      "title": "Director of Global Engagement",
      "description": "Director of Global Engagement\nBatten University\n\nBatten University invites applications for the position of Director of Global Engagement. The position is a full-\ntime, 12-month staff position that reports to the Provost and Vice President. The Director of Global\nEngagement’s primary responsibilities are to administer study away experience, both short and long term, and\nto support international students on campus. The director coordinates study away programs and assists faculty\nwith the development and offering of domestic and international study away courses. The Director also serves\nas the Principal Designated School Official (PDSO) and Responsible Officer (RO), administering the\nuniversity’s F-1 and J-1 programs and ensuring institutional compliance with applicable federal immigration\nregulations and reporting requirements.",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://fa-ewic-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/170": {
      "title": "Advancement Associate",
      "description": "Advancement Associate, Coordinator of the Marlin Athletic Fund\nPosition Summary\nBatten University invites applications for a full-time Advancement Associate, Coordinator of the Marlin Athletic Fund. The position will support the University's advancement and fundraising objectives, with primary responsibility for the development and implementation of fundraising strategies supporting the Marlin Athletic Fund and athletics-related advancement\ninitiatives.\nThe Advancement Associate will independently manage an assigned portfolio of prospective and existing donors, evaluate fundraising opportunities, develop donor cultivation and solicitation strategies, and secure philanthropic support. Working collaboratively with University Advancement and Marlin Athletics, the successful candidate will exercise independent judgment\nin determining appropriate fundraising approaches, prioritizing prospective donors, and recommending initiatives that advance institutional fundraising objectives.",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://fa-ewic-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/171": {
      "title": "Controller",
      "description": "Position Description\n\nThe Controller will join the Division of Enterprise Strategy and report to the Chief Operations Officer/Vice President for Enterprise Strategy. The position oversees Batten University's Office of Finance, ensuring accurate, efficient, and accountable financial operations. The Controller directs accounting, financial reporting, internal controls, audits, cash management, and related functions while ensuring compliance with accounting standards and regulatory requirements.\n\nThe Controller exercises independent judgment in evaluating financial operations, implementing policies and procedures, assessing risks, and recommending improvements. The position supports the University's strategic planning and financial sustainability through financial analysis, budgeting, forecasting, and recommendations that promote sound fiscal stewardship and informed institutional decisions.",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://fa-ewic-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/172": {
      "title": "University Advising Coordinator",
      "description": "University Advising Coordinator\nPosition Description\nBatten University invites applications for the position of University Advising Coordinator. The successful candidate will be responsible for developing, coordinating, and managing a comprehensive, student-centered academic advising program for first-year and undeclared students. This position plays an integral role in supporting student success, academic engagement, retention, and the transition to university life through a strategic and holistic approach to academic advising.\n",
      "department": null
    },
